Let the app ask for HDR, and tell it which colorspace the host sends.

Current Steam streams HDR10 to a client that says its display can show it: the streaming
request's display_hdr (23), and HDR10 (5) among the client caps' supported_colorspaces. Both are
newer than ihslib's copy of the protocol, so display_hdr goes out as an unknown field and HDR10 as
a raw enum value. IHS_SessionConfig.enableHdr and IHS_StreamingRequest.displayHdr turn them on.

CStartVideoDataMsg now also carries the stream's colorspace (6), which protobuf-c keeps among the
unknown fields; IHS_StreamVideoConfig.colorspace passes it on, so the app can set up its decoder
for 10-bit video. IHS_UnknownVarint in pb_utils.h reads such a field.

